{"id":"word:hebrew:H7161","type":"word","title":"קֶרֶן","subtitle":"H7161 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a horn (as projecting); by implication, a flask , cornet ; by resemblance. an elephant's tooth (i.e. ivory), a corner (of the altar), a peak (of a mountain), a ray (of light); figuratively, power","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to קֶרֶן (H7161) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f n-pr-loc.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 76 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"קֶרֶן (qeren) means a horn (as projecting); by implication, a flask , cornet ; by resemblance. an elephant's tooth (i.e. ivory), a corner (of the altar), a peak (of a mountain), a ray (of light); figuratively, power First listed occurrence: 1Chr 25 5."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"קֶרֶן","transliteration":"qeren","pronunciation":"keh'-ren","strong":"H7161","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7161","partOfSpeech":"n-f n-pr-loc","forms":["קֶ֣רֶן","קַרְנֹתָ֑י/ו","קַרְנֵ֣י","קֶ֥רֶן","קַרְנ֣וֹת"],"morphs":[["HNcbpc",14],["HNcbpc/Sp3ms",10],["HNcbsa",7],["HNcbsc",7],["HR/Ncbpc",3],["HNcbdc",3],["HNcbsc/Sp1cs",3],["HTd/Ncbpa",3],["HC/Ncbsc",2],["HNcbda",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"a horn (as projecting); by implication, a flask , cornet ; by resemblance. an elephant's tooth (i.e. ivory), a corner (of the altar), a peak (of a mountain), a ray (of light); figuratively, power","usage":"× hill, horn.","full":"H7161. qeren קֶ֫רֶן 75 noun feminine Jer 48:25 horn ; — absolute ׳ק Isa 5:1 +, קָ֑רֶן Psa 75:5 ; construct קֶ֫רֶן Josh 6:5 +; suffix קַרְנִי 1Sam 2:1 ; Psa 92:11 , etc.; dual קַרְנַיִם Hab 3:4 , קְרָנַיִם Dan 8:3 , 6 , נָ֑יִם - 8:3 ; 8:20 ; construct קַרְנֵי 1Kin 22:11 +, suffix קַרְנָיו Gen 22:13 ; Deut 33:17 , קְרָנָיו Dan 8:7 , קַרְנֵיכֶם Ezek 34:21 ; plural (usually in derived senses) קְרָנוֺת 43:15 +; construct קַרְנֹת Exod 29:12 +, suffix קַרְנֹתָיו 27:2 +, etc.; — horn: 1. a. of ram ( אַיִל ) Gen 22:13 , so in Daniel's vision Dan 8:3 (twice in verse); 8:6-7 , 20 , and (of goat) 8:5 ; 8:8 ; 8:9 ; 8:21 ; of oppressors in Israel (under figure of rams) Ezek 34:21 , so of nations Zech 2:2 ; 2:4 (3 t. in verse); of רְאֵם Deut 33:17 ; Psa 22:22 (both figurative, compare 92:11 ); of Zion under figure of threshing-ox Micah 4:13 ; ׳ק בַּרְזֶל 1Kin 22:11 2Chr 18:10 (symbolic); seen in Zechariah's vision Zech 2:1 . b. used as oil-flask 1Sam 16:1 , 13 ; 1Kin 1:39 (compare הַמּוּח קֶרֶן below). c. ׳ק הַיּוֺבֵל , as wind-instrument Josh 6:5 (compare שׁוֺפָר ). d. שֵׁן קַרְנוֺת Ezek 27:15 (from curved shape of tusks). 2 figurative, of person, symbol of strength Deut 33:17 , ׳ק יִשְׁעִי 2Sam 22:3 = Psa 18:3 (of ׳י as deliverer); others below 3 or 4 ; especially as lifted up ( רום , as of a lordly animal, compare Dr 1Samuel 2. 1 ), denoting increase of might, dignity 1Sam 2:1 , 10 ; Lam 2:17 ; Psalm 75:11; Psa 89:18 ; 89:25 ; 92:11 ; 112:9 , so perhaps 1Chr 25:5 (see Kau; &gt; Be blow loudly [compare 1c ]), + לְעַמּוֺ Psa 148:14 (subject ׳י ); also haughtiness, arrogance 75:5 ; 75:6 ; opposed to ק ׳גָּדַע hew off horns , i.e. reduce, humiliate, Lam 2:3 ; Psalm 75:11, passive Jer 48:25 , so קַרְנִי בֶעָפָר וְעֹלַלְתִּי Job 16:15 ; ק ׳אַצְמִיהַ יִשׂ ׳לְבֵית Ezek 29:21 is apparently of restoration of might (as Psa 148:14 above, with וַיָּרֶם ), but ׳אַצ ׳ק לְדָוִד 132:17 of raising up individual ruler of Davidic line. 3 of altar, horn-like projections at corners (26 t.), Amos 3:14 ; Jer 17:1 ; Ezek 43:15 , 20 ; Psa 118:27 ; Exodus 27:22 + 8t. Exodus; Lev 4:7 , 18 6 t. Leviticus (all P); as sanctuary, refuge 1Kin 1:50-51 , 2:28 . 4 hill (so in Arabic, peak, isolated hill , compare Ges) Isa 5:1 . 5 לוֺ מִיָּדוֺ קַרְנַיִם Hab 3:4 rays at his side(s) had he (of lightning-flashes in theoph., compare Now Da). — Amos 6:13 see קַדְנַיִם proper name, of a location קַרְנַ֫יִם proper name, of a location conquered by Israel Amos 6:13 (so Gr We Now GASm, compare also דְבָר לֹא above; ᵐ5 and most below קֶרֶן 2 ); probably in Bashan, = Καρναιν 1Macc 5:43; 5:44, Καρνιον 2Macc 12:21; also in ק ׳עַשְׁתְּרוֺת Gen 14:5 (see III. עַשְׁתָּרוֺת above). קֶ֫רֶן noun feminine Dan 7:8 horn (see Biblical Hebrew קרן ); — absolute ׳ק 7:8 ; emphatic קַרְנָא 3:5 +; dual (often !) קַרְנַ֫יִן 7:7 ; emphatic נַיָּא - 7:8 +; — 1 instrument of music, Dan 3:5 , 7 , 10 , 15 . 2 symbolic, in vision , Dan 7:7-8 , (3 t. in verse); 7:11 , 20 (twice in verse); 7:21 , 24 .","rootNote":"from 7160 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 25 5","keyReferences":["1Chr 25 5","1Kgs 1 39","1Kgs 1 50","1Kgs 1 51","1Kgs 2 28","1Kgs 22 11","1Sam 2 1","1Sam 2 10"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":76,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 25 5","book":"1Chr","chapter":25,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"קָ֑רֶן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 39","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":39,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"קֶ֤רֶן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 50","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":50,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/קַרְנ֥וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncbpc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 51","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":51,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/קַרְנ֤וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncbpc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 28","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":28,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּ/קַרְנ֥וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncbpc"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 11","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"קַרְנֵ֣י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbdc"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 1","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"קַרְנִ֖/י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"1Sam 2 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":2,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"קֶ֥רֶן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc"},{"reference":"1Sam 16 1","book":"1Sam","chapter":16,"verse